BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Indie Press Fiction Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T190000
UID:bm-6781920261123@shop.benmcnallybooks.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/7600763/Website2/
 Events/2026_11_23.png?cb=1794585263
DESCRIPTION:[at Ben McNally Books]\nJoin us at Ben McNally Books\, for an 
 evening of Indie Press fiction\, featuring Stella Harvey\, Jon Redfern\, a
 nd Denise Roig.\nAbout the Books:\nDisruption\nby Stella Leventoyannis Ha
 rvey\nYoung Kitianna has always been curious about what life is like on th
 e other side of the wall that divides her war-scarred country. When her ac
 tions draw the scrutiny of the authorities\, Kitianna’s parents realize 
 the only way to keep her from being forced into a re-education camp is to 
 send her away.\nBut while they may have secured their daughter’s safety\
 , at least for now\, the underground protest movement against the governme
 nt is getting stronger\, and the regime’s reaction has been to double do
 wn on draconian security measures. It seems no one is safe from the droids
  and the drones and the surveillance that is everywhere.\nDisruption\nasks
  how much freedom we’re willing to relinquish for the sake of security. 
 And when the government is secretly controlled by oligarchs\, how can ordi
 nary citizens fight back and reclaim their liberties?\nThe Ogre Club\nby J
 on Redfern\nRichard Suttle's just taken a detour from his quiet life as a 
 fraud investigator in Winnipeg--into the heart of Mexico City's dark under
 world. His mission? Find Brendan Thorst\, the reckless 22-year-old son of 
 his ailing high school friend.\nBrendan's no saint. He's a spoiled trouble
 maker who vanished after raising the ire of brutal cartels and street deal
 ers by selling drugs to unsuspecting tourists. But that's only the surface
 .\nThe real story is far more twisted--and deadly. Brendan's on the run af
 ter threatening to expose a powerful televangelist who's hiding a horrifyi
 ng secret: a kiddy porn operation protected by corrupt cops and blind fait
 h.\nNow Suttle must navigate a lethal maze of deception\, violence\, and b
 etrayal. Because in this city\, the only thing more dangerous than the cri
 minals is the man who's supposed to be on your side.\nGathered Here\nby De
 nise Roig\nIs it too late to make peace with one’s choices?\nTo marry or
  not to marry.\nThree generations of women in southern Ontario ponder what
 ’s in it for them. Karin\, a millennial\, her fifty-something Aunt Sheen
 a\, and Jane\, Karin’s grandmother\, narrate their separate\, but linked
 \, stories of love\, weddings\, loss\, and a little mayhem.\nCan love – 
 imperfect\, unpredictable\, human – really conquer all?
LOCATION:Ben McNally Books
URL:https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events
X-SOURCE:Ben McNally Books
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:45 Books in 45 Minutes\, Winter 2026 Edition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261125T193000
UID:bm-6576620261125@shop.benmcnallybooks.com
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://cdn1.bookmanager.com/i/7600763/Website2/
 Events/2026_W45.png?cb=1791993349
DESCRIPTION:[Online Presentation]\nA contingent of McNallys will be blazin
 g through a selection of 45 (or so) new releases of the season in (about) 
 45 minutes.\nIt's the perfect opportunity to find some books for everyone 
 on your list. And\, better yet\, if you're really careful\, you can read i
 t first before you give it away. We won't tell anyone!\nThe important thin
 g is that we'll be going over some history\, biography\, thrillers\, movin
 g fiction\, and various non-fiction. Just enough to give you a taste of th
 e multitude of good books that are out there.\nFor those of you who aren't
  able to tune in on the day\, we'll have a recording available for about a
  month afterwards for those who have purchased a ticket.\nPlease note: thi
 s is for the online event! The tickets say 'in store' as a way to denote b
 eing 'in stock.' It's also worth mentioning that you can chose 'pick up' o
 r 'ship.' Either way\, since there is no physical ticket\, we will neither
  charge you for shipping nor require you to pick one up. We'll simply emai
 l you a confirmation and sign you up for the Zoom session.
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://shop.benmcnallybooks.com/events
X-SOURCE:Ben McNally Books
END:VEVENT
